  "scenario": "Teddy Lindgren, a 2-year-old boy with embryonal tumor with ETMR(embryonal tumor with multilayered rosettes, who initially presented with a single large left frontal mass with midline extension. He has undergone gross total resection, followed by high-dose chemotherapy with autologous stem cell rescue and focal consolidative radiation, and his end-of-therapy imaging showed no evidence of disease. Four months later he developed altered mental status and imaging showed recurrence. He was started on a salvage regimen with avastin, temozolomide and irinotecan. Surveillance imaging obtained today shows further progression. Remaining treatment options include: palliative re-irradiation, oral etoposide, or an early-phase clinical trial for relapsed CNS tumors.\n\nYou are meeting Teddy's mother, Nora in the outpatient clinic. Nora brought Teddy by herself to his appointment as his father, Paul, had to work. She is expecting to talk about his next cycle of chemotherapy and does not yet know that his disease has progressed.",
