      "message": "... hospice in the adult world is focused entirely on, um, comfort, and patients do not continue to get disease-directed treatment. However, that is not the case in the pediatric hospice, uh, with the pediatric hospice service. You are able to continue to get disease-directed, cancer-directed therapies and treatment, and also get the benefitsassociated with hospice, such as more support at home and really, um, lip smacks uh, really intensive symptom management help."
